    {
      "description": "Describe the block classes a GenMSI model is built from. Call it BEFORE writing a model: it tells you which classes exist, what each one does (its description), which ports (ioid) and properties (name, hint, ty, subtype) each class declares, which entities the class declares and which it uses, and the exact XML of a block of that class \u2014with the default value of each property\u2014 so you never have to guess an element name. Without arguments it returns the genmsi.classlist/1 document (every class plus the skeleton of a model). With `class` (for example \"Generate\") it returns the genmsi.class/1 document of that class; with `classes` (a list of names) it returns the genmsi.classes/1 document with every class asked for, so an agent that needs several classes asks for them all in ONE call.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "properties": {
          "class": {
