      "description": "Say which model the GenMSI desktop app has open, so you do not have to guess where to write it. It returns the genmsi.openmodel/1 document: `path` is the absolute path of the file the app has open and `pid` is the process that has it open; both are null when the app is not running. Write the model to that path (with save_model) and the app, which watches the file it has open, reloads it and runs it again, so the reader sees the change.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {},
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "open_model"
    },
    {
      "description": "Write a GPSS model to a .gmdl file. The model is checked before it is written: one that does not load, does not validate or does not compile is NOT written, and the error names the block that caused it. A model that carries no canvas geometry is composed before it is written, so the editor can draw it; a model that already carries its geometry keeps the disposition its author left. Takes `model` (the whole .gmdl document as text, not a patch) and `path` (the file to write): `path` may be left out, and then the model the app has open is the one that is written. `target` says where the model goes: `file` (the default) writes it to that file, and `proposal` leaves the model in the staging area of the app, without touching the disk (the `path` is not written to), where the person sees it and decides to accept it or to discard it \u2014 the verdict comes back in `app_state`. `summary` is one line about what the agent did; it travels with the proposal. Returns the genmsi.lint/1 document of what was written. Use it to create or to change a model: read it first with explain_model, change the text and hand the complete document back.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "Target": {
